	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/mouse_settings/help_strings">
		<string text="The mouse, the controller and the keys."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="How far the view turns as the mouse moves, on Counter-Strike 2's scale: your CS2 number turns the same here. Drag the slider, or press left and right. Click the number (or press A) to type an exact value, e.g. 1.7, then press Enter.|No acceleration."/>
		<string text="How far the view turns up and down, of how far it turns side to side. 1X turns it as far."/>
		<string text="How fast you turn while zoomed in. CS2 matches Counter-Strike 2's scoped feel; Original is how Halo felt.|Mouse only: controllers always turn as Halo did."/>
		<string text="Moving the mouse forward looks down, as a flight stick does."/>
		<string text="Slows and drags your aim along with a target while you aim with the mouse, as it does with a controller."/>
		<string text="Turns the view the moment the mouse moves, not up to two of the game's updates later. Off feels as the original did."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="The look sensitivity and inversion, the button and stick layouts, and vibration, kept in your player profile."/>
		<string text="Hold crouches while the button is held, as Halo did. Toggle crouches at a tap until you press it again, jump, take a seat or die; holding it still crouches while held.|A full push of the stick keeps you crouched either way."/>
		<string text="The touch controls' Crouch. Toggle crouches at a tap until the next tap, a jump, a seat or death; Hold crouches while your finger is on it."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="The keys and mouse buttons for each action, two for each."/>
		<string text="The buttons the HUD's prompts show. Auto shows the keys or the controller's buttons, as you last played with."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Your hands, aiming, turning, your height, the HUD and the menus in VR."/>
	</strings>
